  "label": "The unborn child is mapped as a bomb",
  "description": "The text 'it's a bomb' is an analogical mapping that projects the unborn child (implied by the pregnant woman's belly being touched) onto the metaphorical concept of a bomb. The visual of the pregnant woman's belly, the focal point of the pregnancy reveal, is mapped onto the textual entity 'bomb', creating a shocking and violent analogy. This mapping is central to the meme's dark humor and harmful intent, as it devalues the child by equating it with destruction.",
